# Netlify rules. The first rule that matches wins.
#
# `/` is the product page. The `!` is necessary: `index.html` (the web app)
# exists at `/`, and without `!` Netlify serves that file and skips the rule.
/              /site/index.html   200!
# The web app. Its library is at `/app` (Router.homePath). Every other path,
# for example `/diagrams/<id>` and `/example/<slug>`, opens the app too.
/diagrams/*    /index.html        200
/*             /index.html        200
